--- kv — key-value store abstraction for the handl runtime.
---
--- This is a trait-abstraction library: the KeyValueStore trait lives in
--- Rust (plugin-lib-kv) and is implemented by concrete backend crates
--- (kv-hashmap). The kv.* functions (kv.get, kv.set, kv.remove, kv.has,
--- kv.clear, kv.size) are callable from handl expressions via the impl
--- crate's op/handl bindings. This .hnl file declares the library's
--- capability surface for the plugin system.
